---
name: Bichon Frise
ingredients:
  - type: Vodka
    amount: '1.5'
    unit: oz
    garnish: false
  - type: Red grapefruit juice
    amount: '1'
    unit: oz
    garnish: false
  - type: Elderflower liqueur
    amount: 3/4
    unit: oz
    garnish: false
  - type: Lemon juice
    amount: 1/4
    unit: oz
    garnish: false
  - type: Vanilla Rim Sugar
    amount: '1'
    unit: count
    garnish: true
category:
  - vodka
image: ../../images/cocktails/bichon-frise/image.jpg
sourceUrl: https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/13508-bichon-frise
---
1. Spread sugar, if using, into even layer on small saucer. Moisten about ½ inch of chilled cocktail glass rim by running grapefruit wedge around outer edge; dry any excess juice with paper towel. Roll moistened rim in sugar to coat. Remove any excess sugar that falls into glass; set aside.
1. Add vodka, grapefruit juice, liqueur, and lemon juice to cocktail shaker, then fill with ice. Shake mixture until fully combined and well chilled, about 15 seconds. Double-strain cocktail into prepared glass. Pinch grapefruit peel over drink and, if rim is unsugared, rub outer edge of glass with peel. Garnish with grapefruit peel and serve.
